{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"find / -name apply_patch -type f 2>/dev/null | head; cat references_provenance.json | tail -35; head -65 claims_grounding.json; cat validation_report.json; sed -n '1,150p' validate_artifacts.py; rg --files .codex/skills | head -45; sed -n '1,80p' postdraft_reference_query_plan.md\"","aggregated_output":"      \"citation_key\": \"Efron1979\",\n      \"id\": \"ref.Efron1979\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"doi:10.1214/aos/1176344552\",\n      \"query\": \"Bootstrap Methods: Another Look at the Jackknife\",\n      \"read_artifact\": \"literature/Efron1979.json\",\n      \"read_scope\": \"Exact-title bibliographic record and abstract when available. Citation network not accessed.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1214/aos/1176344552\",\n      \"title\": \"Bootstrap Methods: Another Look at the Jackknife\",\n      \"year\": 1979\n    },\n    {\n      \"citation_key\": \"Brown2001\",\n      \"id\": \"ref.Brown2001\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"doi:10.1214/ss/1009213286\",\n      \"query\": \"Interval Estimation for a Binomial Proportion\",\n      \"read_artifact\": \"literature/Brown2001.json\",\n      \"read_scope\": \"Exact-title bibliographic record and abstract when available. Citation network not accessed.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1214/ss/1009213286\",\n      \"title\": \"Interval Estimation for a Binomial Proportion\",\n      \"year\": 2001\n    },\n    {\n      \"citation_key\": \"Davison1997\",\n      \"id\": \"ref.Davison1997\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"doi:10.1017/cbo9780511802843\",\n      \"query\": \"Bootstrap Methods and their Application\",\n      \"read_artifact\": \"literature/Davison1997.json\",\n      \"read_scope\": \"Exact-title bibliographic record and abstract when available. Citation network not accessed.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1017/CBO9780511802843\",\n      \"title\": \"Bootstrap Methods and their Application\",\n      \"year\": 1997\n    }\n  ],\n  \"results_dir\": \"work/results/r02/codex/20261117_111421/investigation\"\n}{\n  \"claims\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"The independent final evaluation completed, was qualified, and reports successful specified checks; qualification is not a superiority or shifted-validity result.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.qualification.status\",\n        \"final.qualification.outcome\",\n        \"final.qualification.correct\",\n        \"final.metric.control_check_pass_rate\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"The final study comprises eight seeds, six conditions (logistic-normal IID, Dirichlet IID, shifted Dirichlet at K=3 and 8), and alpha=0.05,0.10,0.20. All recorded cases are complete.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"supporting_artifacts\": [\n        \"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:37\",\n        \"source_evidence/data_manifest.json\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_locator\": \"/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Final seeds are 1009,1013,1019,1021,1031,1033,1039,1049; train/calibration/test sizes are 1024/512/2048 with six covariates.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"supporting_artifacts\": [\n        \"source_evidence/data_manifest.json\",\n        \"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:727\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Positive observed continuous compositions, not categorical labels or latent probabilities, are the response. The fixed Helmert ILR basis has K-1 coordinates.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n        \"result.top_program_01\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"supporting_artifacts\": [\n        \"source_evidence/selected_model.py:37\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"The design uses intercept, raw features, squares, sines and x0*x1. Center and log-residual ridge penalties are 1 and 10; intercept penalty is 1e-8; residual floor is .02.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n        \"result.top_program_01\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"supporting_artifacts\": [\n        \"source_evidence/selected_model.py:98\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Centers are clipped to [-100,100] and positive base and corrected scales to [1e-4,100]. The base log-residual fit uses in-sample residuals; correction moments are cross-fitted.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n        \"result.top_program_01\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"supporting_artifacts\": [\n{\n  \"status\": \"independent_artifact_checks_passed\",\n  \"hard_errors\": [],\n  \"scope\": \"Local source, canonical schemas, rendered PDF, retained-metric consistency and evidence links; not a claim that unavailable parent orchestration checks ran.\",\n  \"body_pages\": 9,\n  \"total_pages\": 16,\n  \"references_start_page\": 10,\n  \"supplement_start_page\": 12,\n  \"reference_count\": 25,\n  \"claim_count\": 102,\n  \"figure_count\": 4,\n  \"dangling_evidence_references\": 0,\n  \"last_body_content_bounds_pt\": [\n    84.17748260498047,\n    572.6866455078125\n  ],\n  \"last_body_fill_note\": \"Bounds are descriptive, not the authoritative parent geometric-occupancy verdict. Body has nine pages, so the special eight-page minimum-fill condition is not invoked.\",\n  \"compiled_inputs_union_check\": {\n    \"passed\": true,\n    \"recorded_input_count\": 262\n  },\n  \"qualification\": {\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"outcome\": \"qualified\",\n    \"correct\": true\n  },\n  \"environment_limitations\": [\n    \"Canonical validate_figures.py cannot import src.orchestrator.paper_step in this isolated workspace. The shipped canonical figure schema, required figure IDs, source paths and strategy density budgets were checked independently.\",\n    \"Canonical compile_latex.sh input guard rejects /usr/share/texmf/web2c/texmf.cnf because it is a system symlink into a different approved system tree. No validator or system symlink was modified. Sanitized pdflatex/bibtex passes compiled the PDF; all recorded inputs independently resolve inside the workspace or the union of approved system TeX roots.\"\n  ],\n  \"orchestrator_pending\": [\n    \"Replace the intentional conceptual-overview placeholder and prompt-log stub with the synchronous concept render, then perform the parent final compile and authoritative layout checks.\"\n  ]\n}import hashlib\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\nimport jsonschema\nimport pymupdf\n\n\ndef main():\n    root = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    manifest = json.loads(Path('figure_manifest.json').read_text())\n    schema = json.loads(Path('.codex/skills/validate-paper/templates/figure_manifest.schema.json').read_text())\n    jsonschema.validate(manifest, schema)\n    strategy = json.loads(Path('paper_strategy.json').read_text())\n    planned = {figure['figure_id']: figure for figure in strategy['figure_specs']}\n    actual = {figure['figure_id']: figure for figure in manifest['figures']}\n    for figure_id, specification in planned.items():\n        assert figure_id in actual\n        figure = actual[figure_id]\n        assert figure['panel_count'] <= specification['max_panels']\n        assert all(panel['category_count'] <= specification['max_categories_per_panel'] and\n                   panel['series_count'] <= specification['max_series_per_panel'] for panel in figure['panels'])\n        assert figure['placement'] == 'full_width'\n    tex = Path('paper.tex').read_text()\n    graphics = set(re.findall(r'\\\\includegraphics(?:\\[[^\\]]*\\])?\\{([^}]+)\\}', tex))\n    registered = {path for figure in manifest['figures'] for path in figure['files'].values()}\n    assert graphics <= registered\n    assert all(Path(path).is_file() for path in registered)\n    for path in ('analysis/coverage_table.tex', 'analysis/complete_comparisons.tex'):\n        assert Path(path).read_text().strip() in tex\n    bibliography_keys = set(re.findall(r'@\\w+\\{([^,]+),', Path('references.bib').read_text()))\n    assert 25 <= len(bibliography_keys) <= 30\n    cited = {key.strip() for group in re.findall(r'\\\\cite\\w*\\{([^}]+)\\}', tex) for key in group.split(',')}\n    assert cited == bibliography_keys\n    provenance = json.loads(Path('references_provenance.json').read_text())\n    assert cited == {reference['citation_key'] for reference in provenance['references']}\n    assert all(Path(reference['read_artifact']).is_file() for reference in provenance['references'])\n    claims = json.loads(Path('claims_grounding.json').read_text())['claims']\n    evidence_anchor = '@evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]'\n    payload = json.loads(Path('paper_data.json').read_text())\n    summary = json.loads(Path('analysis/summary.json').read_text())\n    for metric, summary_key in (('iid_coverage_error', 'iid_error'), ('shift_coverage_error', 'shift_error'),\n                                ('mean_volume', 'mass'), ('final_score', 'utility')):\n        assert abs(payload['final_evaluation']['metrics'][metric] - summary['methods']['scaled_ilr'][summary_key]) < 1e-12\n    assert abs(payload['final_evaluation']['metrics']['baseline_utility_gap'] -\n               summary['paired_overall']['simplex_linf']['mean']) < 1e-12\n    for key in ('status', 'outcome', 'correct'):\n        assert summary['qualification'][key] == payload['final_evaluation'][key]\n    selected_path = Path('results/ideas/03_training_only_conformal_rank_scale_selection/program_1/src/program.py')\n    assert Path('source_evidence/selected_model.py').read_bytes() == selected_path.read_bytes()\n    assert Path('source_evidence/evaluate_final.py').read_bytes() == Path('task/evaluate_final.py').read_bytes()\n    registry = set(payload['grounding_sources']) | {reference['id'] for reference in provenance['references']}\n    assert all(set(claim['source_ids']) <= registry for claim in claims)\n    summary = json.loads(Path('analysis/summary.json').read_text())\n    final = payload['final_evaluation']\n    for name, derived in [('iid_coverage_error', 'iid_error'), ('shift_coverage_error', 'shift_error'),\n                          ('mean_volume', 'mass'), ('final_score', 'utility')]:\n        assert abs(final['metrics'][name] - summary['methods']['scaled_ilr'][derived]) < 1e-12\n    assert summary['qualification'] == {key: final[key] for key in ('status', 'outcome', 'correct')}\n    assert final['outcome'] == 'qualified'\n    selected_source = Path('results/ideas/03_training_only_conformal_rank_scale_selection/program_1/src/program.py')\n    assert selected_source.read_bytes() == Path('source_evidence/selected_model.py').read_bytes()\n    assert Path('task/evaluate_final.py').read_bytes() == Path('source_evidence/evaluate_final.py').read_bytes()\n    verified = json.loads(Path('scientific-evidence/verification-report.json').read_text())\n    assert verified['summary']['dangling_references'] == 0\n    document = pymupdf.open('paper.pdf')\n    texts = [page.get_text() for page in document]\n    reference_index = next(index for index, text in enumerate(texts) if re.search(r'(?m)^REFERENCES\\s*$', text))\n    supplement_index = next(index for index, text in enumerate(texts) if 'SUPPLEMENTARY INFORMATION' in text)\n    assert 8 <= reference_index <= 9\n    assert supplement_index > reference_index\n    visible = '\\n'.join(texts)\n    prohibited = ('idea', 'ideas', 'program', 'programs', 'attempt', 'attempts', 'eligible', 'combined_score',\n                  'rubric', 'worker_01', 'worker_02')\n    assert not any(re.search(r'\\b' + token + r'\\b', visible, re.I) for token in prohibited)\n    assert 'LLM USAGE' in visible\n    assert 'Anonymous authors' in texts[0]\n    assert not re.search(r'Overfull \\\\[hv]box|undefined', Path('paper.log').read_text(), re.I)\n    validator_path = Path('.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_rendered_si.py')\n    specification = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('rendered_si', validator_path)\n    validator = importlib.util.module_from_spec(specification)\n    specification.loader.exec_module(validator)\n    extracted = subprocess.run(['pdftotext', '-layout', 'paper.pdf', '-'], check=True, capture_output=True, text=True)\n    assert not validator.validate_rendered_supplementary_information(extracted.stdout.split('\\f'))\n    recorded_inputs = []\n    system_roots = [Path(path).resolve() for path in ('/etc/texmf', '/usr/share/texmf', '/usr/share/texlive', '/var/lib/texmf')]\n    for line in Path('paper.fls').read_text().splitlines():\n        if not line.startswith('INPUT '):\n            continue\n        resolved = Path(line[6:]).resolve()\n        assert resolved.is_relative_to(root) or any(resolved.is_relative_to(system_root) for system_root in system_roots), str(resolved)\n        recorded_inputs.append(str(resolved))\n    last_body = document[reference_index-1]\n    bounds = [span['bbox'] for block in last_body.get_text('dict')['blocks'] if block['type'] == 0\n              for line in block['lines'] for span in line['spans']\n              if span['bbox'][0] >= 107 and 65 < span['bbox'][1] < 715]\n    report = {\n        'status': 'independent_artifact_checks_passed', 'hard_errors': [],\n        'scope': 'Local source, canonical schemas, rendered PDF, retained-metric consistency and evidence links; not a claim that unavailable parent orchestration checks ran.',\n        'body_pages': reference_index, 'total_pages': len(document),\n        'references_start_page': reference_index+1, 'supplement_start_page': supplement_index+1,\n        'reference_count': len(cited), 'claim_count': len(claims), 'figure_count': len(actual),\n        'dangling_evidence_references': verified['summary']['dangling_references'],\n        'last_body_content_bounds_pt': [min(bound[1] for bound in bounds), max(bound[3] for bound in bounds)],\n        'last_body_fill_note': 'Bounds are descriptive, not the authoritative parent geometric-occupancy verdict. Body has nine pages, so the special eight-page minimum-fill condition is not invoked.',\n        'compiled_inputs_union_check': {'passed': True, 'recorded_input_count': len(recorded_inputs)},\n        'qualification': summary['qualification'],\n        'environment_limitations': [\n            'Canonical validate_figures.py cannot import src.orchestrator.paper_step in this isolated workspace. The shipped canonical figure schema, required figure IDs, source paths and strategy density budgets were checked independently.',\n            'Canonical compile_latex.sh input guard rejects /usr/share/texmf/web2c/texmf.cnf because it is a system symlink into a different approved system tree. No validator or system symlink was modified. Sanitized pdflatex/bibtex passes compiled the PDF; all recorded inputs independently resolve inside the workspace or the union of approved system TeX roots.'\n        ],\n        'orchestrator_pending': ['Replace the intentional conceptual-overview placeholder and prompt-log stub with the synchronous concept render, then perform the parent final compile and authoritative layout checks.']\n    }\n    Path('validation_report.json').write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=2))\n    print(json.dumps(report, indent=2))\n    template_source = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ICLR/Master-Template/master/iclr2026/'\n    Path('template_provenance.json').write_text(json.dumps({\n        'venue': 'ICLR 2026', 'anonymous_review': True,\n        'files': [{'path': name, 'source_url': template_source+name,\n                   'sha256': hashlib.sha256(Path(name).read_bytes()).hexdigest()}\n                  for name in ('iclr2026_conference.sty', 'iclr2026_conference.bst')]}, indent=2))\n    for name, kind, sources in [\n        ('paper.tex', 'manuscript', ['paper_data.json', 'claims_grounding.json', 'references.bib', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py']),\n        ('paper.pdf', 'manuscript', ['paper.tex', 'references.bib', 'figure_manifest.json']),\n        ('figure_manifest.json', 'derived', ['paper_strategy.json', 'build_analysis.py']),\n        ('validation_report.json', 'derived', ['paper.tex', 'paper.pdf', 'scientific-evidence/verification-report.json'])]:\n        sidecar = {'schema_name': 'scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest',\n                   'artifact': {'path': name, 'kind': kind},\n                   'derived_from': ['@'+'evidence[['+source+']]' for source in sources]}\n        if name == 'paper.pdf':\n            sidecar['generated_by'] = {\n                'script_path': '.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_compile_inputs.py',\n                'command': ['python', '.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_compile_inputs.py',\n                            'run', '--', 'pdflatex', '-recorder', '-no-shell-escape',\n                            '-interaction=nonstopmode', '-halt-on-error', 'paper.tex']}\n        elif name != 'paper.tex':\n            sidecar['generated_by'] = {'script_path': 'build_analysis.py' if name == 'figure_manifest.json' else 'validate_artifacts.py'}\n        else:\n            sidecar['notes'] = 'Manuscript authored during the paper-writing workflow; this sidecar records its source trail, not an automated manuscript generator.'\n        Path(name+'.prov.json').write_text(json.dumps(sidecar, indent=2))\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n.codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh\n.codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.py\n.codex/skills/scientific-evidence/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\n.codex/skills/memory-log/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_compile_inputs.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_rendered_si.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/__pycache__/validate_rendered_si.cpython-312.pyc\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/scripts/openalex_fetch.py\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/scripts/scholarly_fetch.py\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/scripts/s2_fetch.py\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/templates/provenance.schema.json\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/generate-concept-figure/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/templates/figure_manifest.schema.json\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/claims_grounding.schema.json\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/alife/alifeconf.sty\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/alife/paper.tex\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/references.bib\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.bst\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.sty\n# Post-draft incremental reference query plan\n\n**Status:** ready\n\n## Topic and scope\n\nSupply direct multivariate conformal context for the existing joint simplex-coordinate maximum-residual and coordinatewise Bonferroni comparators in the study of scale-adaptive split-conformal regions for observed positive continuous compositions. This is an attribution and positioning task, not a literature refresh, a new experiment, or a missing validity proof.\n\nThe primary drivers, `draft_reference_gaps.md` and `draft_reference_gaps.json`, identify exactly one medium-priority target: `multivariate-rectangular-comparators`. The bounded destination is **Prediction Regions and Evaluation Targets → Compared region constructions**, `paper.tex:85`, anchored by “The latter is a simultaneous-coordinate baseline”.\n\n**Budget: two focused queries, aiming for one or two citations total.** The single gap and its two explicit search topics justify fewer than the default three to six queries. Both queries address the same paragraph, but distinguish joint-score construction from coordinatewise multiplicity correction. A single source supporting both constructions can close the gap; do not seek one new reference per query.\n\n## Grounding and existing coverage\n\nReviewed the two gap artifacts first, then `paper.tex`, `references.bib`, `references_provenance.json`, `global_memory_summary.md`, and the schema and exclusions in `reference_query_plan.json`. The memory summary supplies qualitative context only, not numerical or bibliographic evidence.\n\nThe existing bibliography contains 25 entries with provenance. General conformal foundations and regression calibration are already represented by `Vovk2005`, `Papadopoulos2002`, `Lei2018`, and `Angelopoulos2021`; the draft also cites adaptive scalar-interval work including `Romano2019` and `Sesia2020`. These are context, not evidence that the specific multivariate comparator families have already been directly attributed. The provenance records for these entries report abstract, overview, or metadata-level reading rather than verified full-text support for this paragraph. Do not infer that these sources lack relevant material: downstream, reuse an existing entry if its actual content supports the needed construction before adding a redundant reference. Deduplicate any new candidate against existing titles and DOI/arXiv identifiers.\n\n## Queries\n\n### 1. Joint maximum-residual rectangles\n\n- **Query:** `multivariate split conformal rectangular prediction regions maximum standardized absolute residual score`\n- **Category:** `baseline_comparator`\n- **Rationale:** At `paper.tex:85`, directly contextualize the vector-response rectangular region obtained by jointly calibrating a maximum absolute residual score. A standardized-score formulation is relevant family context, but the implemented **Simplex max** comparator is unscaled; verify that the source supports the unit-scale specialization. This fills a specific comparator-attribution gap rather than repeating a general split-conformal or adaptive scalar-interval search.\n- **Acceptance boundary:** Support must concern simultaneous vector-response regions and joint maximum-score calibration. Cite only verified general constructions; do not imply that the exact simplex-intersected implementation was taken from the source. Reuse an existing suitable bibliography entry where possible.\n\n### 2. Coordinatewise Bonferroni versus joint calibration\n\n- **Query:** `multivariate conformal prediction simultaneous prediction intervals coordinatewise Bonferroni joint maximum residual calibration`\n- **Category:** `baseline_comparator`\n- **Rationale:** At the same paragraph and its simultaneous-coordinate anchor, directly contextualize separate coordinatewise calibration at miscoverage `alpha/K` and distinguish it from a jointly calibrated maximum-residual threshold. This is the multiplicity/simultaneous-coverage aspect of the gap, not another search for adaptive marginal intervals.\n- **Acceptance boundary:** Prefer a source explicitly discussing both constructions; complementary sources can support them separately. Do not claim an efficiency ordering, a new validity theorem, or publication of the exact compositional implementation. One source satisfying both queries is enough.\n\n## Context deliberately not queried\n\n- **Core methods:** Independent split calibration and maximum standardized ILR residuals already have general conformal and compositional support; no additional core-method search is planned.\n- **Comparators:** The targets are exactly the joint simplex-coordinate maximum-absolute-residual region and separate coordinatewise Bonferroni intervals intersected with the simplex. The scaled and unscaled ILR comparisons remain unchanged.\n- **Benchmarks:** The existing synthetic logistic-normal and Dirichlet IID and shifted evaluations supply context only. No dataset or benchmark-context gap was identified.\n- **Architectural shifts and result-driven themes:** No incremental queries are justified. Citation additions cannot establish selector-only effects, conditional or shifted validity, uniform efficiency superiority, or results on unevaluated data or geometries.\n\n## Exclusions and stopping rule\n\nPreserve the original plan's exclusions: no attempt to identify or retrieve the prohibited study or derivative material; no broad joint compositional-conformal discovery, citation-network expansion, cited-by traversal, related-paper recommendations, or unrestricted survey crawling. Keep searches in the separate multivariate-conformal neighborhood without compositional benchmark terms. Do not introduce classification, image/text datasets, latent probabilities, alternative geometries, structural zeros, neural architectures, or architecture transfer as evaluated settings. Do not present weighted conformal, jackknife+, quantile-regression conformal, credal, clustered, or multivalid methods as implemented comparisons. Avoid generic optimization, benchmarking, writing, chronology, or internal scoring searches. Do not search to support unsupported conditional-validity, shift-robustness, superiority, or selector-causality claims.\n\nDo not reopen already-supported calibration, adaptive scaling, compositional geometry, conditional/shifted validity, statistical ingredients, or benchmark topics. Stop once one or two verified sources, including suitable existing entries, directly support both comparator families. The only intended downstream manuscript edit is a short context sentence or citation clause in the existing paragraph; no new experimental method, section, or manuscript reframing is needed. An unsuccessful targeted pass should leave this positioning gap unresolved rather than expand the search or imply support.\n\nNo reference retrieval or network lookup was performed. The manuscript, bibliography, and provenance are unchanged.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
