{j})=g(0). But in either case, we only need to compare the boundaries in order to find the infimum. Therefore, it follows that inf z j ∈ [ 0 , ω j ​ ( Q ^ 1 − α gwc ) ] g ⁡ ( z j ) = min ⁡ { g ⁡ ( 0 ) , lim z j → ω j ​ ( Q ^ 1 − α gwc ) g ⁡ ( z j ) } . \\inf_{z_{j}\\in[0,\\omega_{j}(\\hat{Q}^{\\mathrm{gwc}}_{1-\\alpha})]}g(z_{j})=\\min\\left\\{g(0),\\lim_{z_{j}\\rightarrow\\omega_{j}(\\hat{Q}^{\\mathrm{gwc}}_{1-\\alpha})}g(z_{j})\\right\\}. This is true for every j ∈ [ d ] j\\in[d] , so we must have Φ ^ lwc ​ ( t , h ) \\displaystyle\\hat{\\Phi}^{\\mathrm{lwc}}(t;h) = max 1 ≤ j ≤ d ⁡ { sup z ∈ R h t j σ ^ j ​ ( z j ) − inf z ∈ ℰ gwc g ⁡ ( z j ) } \\displaystyle=\\max_{1\\leq j\\leq d}\\left\\{\\sup_{z\\in R^{h}}\\frac{t_{j}}{\\hat{\\sigma}_{j}(z_{j})}-\\inf_{z\\in\\mathcal{E}^{\\mathrm{gwc}}}g(z_{j})\\right\\} = max 1 ≤ j ≤ d ⁡ { t j m j − min ⁡ { μ ^ j ​ ( 0 ) σ ^ j ​ ( 0 ) , lim z j → ω j ​ ( Q ^ 1 − α gwc ) μ ^ j ​ ( z j ) σ ^ j ​ ( z j ) } } . \\displaystyle=\\max_{1\\leq j\\leq d}\\left\\{\\frac{t_{j}}{m_{j}}-\\min\\left\\{\\frac{\\hat{\\mu}_{j}(0)}{\\hat{\\sigma}_{j}(0)},\\lim_{z_{j}\\rightarrow\\omega_{j}(\\hat{Q}^{\\mathrm{gwc}}_{1-\\alpha})}\\frac{\\hat{\\mu}_{j}(z_{j})}{\\hat{\\sigma}_{j}(z_{j})}\\right\\}\\right\\}. ∎\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
