{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom bs4 import BeautifulSoup\npage=BeautifulSoup(Path('/tmp/comparator_2512.15383.html').read_text(),'html.parser')\nfor element in page.select('.ltx_authors,.ltx_date,.ltx_abstract'): print(element.get_text(' ',strip=True))\nsection=page.find(id='S2.SS6'); print(section.get_text(' ',strip=True)[:7000])\nPY\nsed -n '1,125p' validate_artifacts.py\ncat paper.tex.prov.json claims_grounding.json.prov.json\nsed -n '1,140p' build_claims.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom bs4 import BeautifulSoup\npage=BeautifulSoup(Path('/tmp/comparator_2512.15383.html').read_text(),'html.parser')\nfor element in page.select('.ltx_authors,.ltx_date,.ltx_abstract'): print(element.get_text(' ',strip=True))\nsection=page.find(id='S2.SS6'); print(section.get_text(' ',strip=True)[:7000])\nPY\nsed -n '1,125p' validate_artifacts.py\ncat paper.tex.prov.json claims_grounding.json.prov.json\nsed -n '1,140p' build_claims.py\"","aggregated_output":"Yunjie Fan brianfan@usc.edu Affiliation: Department of Mathematics Affiliation: University of Southern California Affiliation: Los Angeles, CA, USA Matteo Sesia sesia@marshall.usc.edu Affiliation: Department of Data Sciences and Operations Affiliation: Thomas Lord Department of Computer Science University of Southern California Los Angeles, CA, USA\nAbstract We propose a conformal prediction method for constructing tight simultaneous prediction intervals for multiple, potentially related, numerical outputs given a single input. This method can be combined with any multi-target regression model and guarantees finite-sample coverage. It is computationally efficient and yields informative prediction intervals even with limited data. The core idea is a novel coordinate-wise standardization procedure that makes residuals across output dimensions directly comparable, estimating suitable scaling parameters using the calibration data themselves. This does not require modeling of cross-output dependence nor auxiliary sample splitting. Implementing this idea requires overcoming technical challenges associated with transductive or full conformal prediction. Experiments on simulated and real data demonstrate this method can produce tighter prediction intervals than existing baselines while maintaining valid simultaneous coverage.\n2.6 Simple but Unsatisfactory Practical Approaches An intuitive plug-in approximation of the ideal oracle is obtained by replacing the population mean μ ∗ \\mu^{*} and standard deviation σ ∗ \\sigma^{*} parameters in ( 6 ) with their empirical counterparts, μ ^ pi \\hat{\\mu}^{\\mathrm{pi}} and σ ^ pi \\hat{\\sigma}^{\\mathrm{pi}} , evaluated on the calibration data, and then constructing hyper-rectangular prediction sets C ^ pi ​ ( X n + 1 ) \\hat{C}^{\\mathrm{pi}}(X^{n+1}) in the form of ( 3 ) using W j = Q ^ 1 − α pi ⋅ σ ^ j pi + μ ^ j pi W_{j}=\\hat{Q}^{\\mathrm{pi}}_{1-\\alpha}\\cdot\\hat{\\sigma}^{\\mathrm{pi}}_{j}+\\hat{\\mu}^{\\mathrm{pi}}_{j} , where Q ^ 1 − α pi := Q ^ 1 − α ​ ( S pi 1 , … , S pi n ) \\hat{Q}^{\\mathrm{pi}}_{1-\\alpha}:=\\hat{Q}_{1-\\alpha}(S^{1}_{\\mathrm{pi}},\\ldots,S^{n}_{\\mathrm{pi}}) and S pi i := Φ ⁡ ( E i , μ ^ pi , σ ^ pi ) S^{i}_{\\mathrm{pi}}:=\\Phi(E^{i};\\hat{\\mu}^{\\mathrm{pi}},\\hat{\\sigma}^{\\mathrm{pi}}) for all i ∈ [ n ] i\\in[n] . This approach, outlined by Algorithm S3 in Appendix A , tends to perform well in large-samples (as shown empirically in Appendix C ) but lacks finite-sample guarantees.\nIn fact, using a data-dependent transformation Φ \\Phi , which breaks the exchangeability between calibration and test scores in ( S 1 , … , S n + 1 ) (S^{1},\\ldots,S^{n+1}) , violates the key assumption of Theorem 1 . An alternative solution that is also intuitive yet unsatisfactory consists of combining the above plug-in approach with an additional data splitting step that allows one to recover finite-sample guarantees: the location and scale parameter estimates for the transformation function Φ \\Phi , denoted here as μ ^ ds \\hat{\\mu}^{\\mathrm{ds}} and σ ^ ds \\hat{\\sigma}^{\\mathrm{ds}} , are estimated empirically using only a random subset of n 1 < n n_{1}<n observations. The remaining n 2 = n − n 1 n_{2}=n-n_{1} data points are used to evaluate the scores ( S ds 1 , … , S ds n 2 ) (S^{1}_{\\mathrm{ds}},\\ldots,S^{n_{2}}_{\\mathrm{ds}}) and compute Q ^ 1 − α ds := Q ^ 1 − α ​ ( S ds 1 , … , S ds n 2 ) \\hat{Q}^{\\mathrm{ds}}_{1-\\alpha}:=\\hat{Q}_{1-\\alpha}(S^{1}_{\\mathrm{ds}},\\ldots,S^{n_{2}}_{\\mathrm{ds}}) , finally leading to W j = Q ^ 1 − α ds ⋅ σ ^ j ds + μ ^ j ds W_{j}=\\hat{Q}^{\\mathrm{ds}}_{1-\\alpha}\\cdot\\hat{\\sigma}^{\\mathrm{ds}}_{j}+\\hat{\\mu}^{\\mathrm{ds}}_{j} .\nThis approach is outlined by Algorithm S4 in Appendix A .\nWhile it satisfies the key assumption of Theorem 1 , it makes an inefficient use of the data. Since it reduces the effective number of calibration samples roughly by half, it tends to produce more unstable and often wider-than-necessary prediction sets, especially in small-sample regimes. The main contribution of this paper is therefore to overcome this inefficiency. We develop a transductive conformal prediction method that uses a similar standardization idea but avoids wasteful data splitting by reusing the entire calibration data to estimate the scaling parameters, all while retaining finite-sample guarantees and manageable computational costs.\nAchieving this requires resolving several technical challenges, as explained step by step below.\nimport hashlib\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\nimport jsonschema\nimport pymupdf\n\n\ndef main():\n    root = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    manifest = json.loads(Path('figure_manifest.json').read_text())\n    schema = json.loads(Path('.codex/skills/validate-paper/templates/figure_manifest.schema.json').read_text())\n    jsonschema.validate(manifest, schema)\n    strategy = json.loads(Path('paper_strategy.json').read_text())\n    planned = {figure['figure_id']: figure for figure in strategy['figure_specs']}\n    actual = {figure['figure_id']: figure for figure in manifest['figures']}\n    for figure_id, specification in planned.items():\n        assert figure_id in actual\n        figure = actual[figure_id]\n        assert figure['panel_count'] <= specification['max_panels']\n        assert all(panel['category_count'] <= specification['max_categories_per_panel'] and\n                   panel['series_count'] <= specification['max_series_per_panel'] for panel in figure['panels'])\n        assert figure['placement'] == 'full_width'\n    tex = Path('paper.tex').read_text()\n    graphics = set(re.findall(r'\\\\includegraphics(?:\\[[^\\]]*\\])?\\{([^}]+)\\}', tex))\n    registered = {path for figure in manifest['figures'] for path in figure['files'].values()}\n    assert graphics <= registered\n    assert all(Path(path).is_file() for path in registered)\n    for path in ('analysis/coverage_table.tex', 'analysis/complete_comparisons.tex'):\n        assert Path(path).read_text().strip() in tex\n    bibliography_keys = set(re.findall(r'@\\w+\\{([^,]+),', Path('references.bib').read_text()))\n    assert 25 <= len(bibliography_keys) <= 30\n    cited = {key.strip() for group in re.findall(r'\\\\cite\\w*\\{([^}]+)\\}', tex) for key in group.split(',')}\n    assert cited == bibliography_keys\n    provenance = json.loads(Path('references_provenance.json').read_text())\n    assert cited == {reference['citation_key'] for reference in provenance['references']}\n    assert all(Path(reference['read_artifact']).is_file() for reference in provenance['references'])\n    claims = json.loads(Path('claims_grounding.json').read_text())['claims']\n    evidence_anchor = '@evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]'\n    payload = json.loads(Path('paper_data.json').read_text())\n    summary = json.loads(Path('analysis/summary.json').read_text())\n    for metric, summary_key in (('iid_coverage_error', 'iid_error'), ('shift_coverage_error', 'shift_error'),\n                                ('mean_volume', 'mass'), ('final_score', 'utility')):\n        assert abs(payload['final_evaluation']['metrics'][metric] - summary['methods']['scaled_ilr'][summary_key]) < 1e-12\n    assert abs(payload['final_evaluation']['metrics']['baseline_utility_gap'] -\n               summary['paired_overall']['simplex_linf']['mean']) < 1e-12\n    for key in ('status', 'outcome', 'correct'):\n        assert summary['qualification'][key] == payload['final_evaluation'][key]\n    selected_path = Path('results/ideas/03_training_only_conformal_rank_scale_selection/program_1/src/program.py')\n    assert Path('source_evidence/selected_model.py').read_bytes() == selected_path.read_bytes()\n    assert Path('source_evidence/evaluate_final.py').read_bytes() == Path('task/evaluate_final.py').read_bytes()\n    registry = set(payload['grounding_sources']) | {reference['id'] for reference in provenance['references']}\n    assert all(set(claim['source_ids']) <= registry for claim in claims)\n    summary = json.loads(Path('analysis/summary.json').read_text())\n    final = payload['final_evaluation']\n    for name, derived in [('iid_coverage_error', 'iid_error'), ('shift_coverage_error', 'shift_error'),\n                          ('mean_volume', 'mass'), ('final_score', 'utility')]:\n        assert abs(final['metrics'][name] - summary['methods']['scaled_ilr'][derived]) < 1e-12\n    assert summary['qualification'] == {key: final[key] for key in ('status', 'outcome', 'correct')}\n    assert final['outcome'] == 'qualified'\n    selected_source = Path('results/ideas/03_training_only_conformal_rank_scale_selection/program_1/src/program.py')\n    assert selected_source.read_bytes() == Path('source_evidence/selected_model.py').read_bytes()\n    assert Path('task/evaluate_final.py').read_bytes() == Path('source_evidence/evaluate_final.py').read_bytes()\n    verified = json.loads(Path('scientific-evidence/verification-report.json').read_text())\n    assert verified['summary']['dangling_references'] == 0\n    document = pymupdf.open('paper.pdf')\n    texts = [page.get_text() for page in document]\n    reference_index = next(index for index, text in enumerate(texts) if re.search(r'(?m)^REFERENCES\\s*$', text))\n    supplement_index = next(index for index, text in enumerate(texts) if 'SUPPLEMENTARY INFORMATION' in text)\n    assert 8 <= reference_index <= 9\n    assert supplement_index > reference_index\n    visible = '\\n'.join(texts)\n    prohibited = ('idea', 'ideas', 'program', 'programs', 'attempt', 'attempts', 'eligible', 'combined_score',\n                  'rubric', 'worker_01', 'worker_02')\n    assert not any(re.search(r'\\b' + token + r'\\b', visible, re.I) for token in prohibited)\n    assert 'LLM USAGE' in visible\n    assert 'Anonymous authors' in texts[0]\n    assert not re.search(r'Overfull \\\\[hv]box|undefined', Path('paper.log').read_text(), re.I)\n    validator_path = Path('.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_rendered_si.py')\n    specification = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('rendered_si', validator_path)\n    validator = importlib.util.module_from_spec(specification)\n    specification.loader.exec_module(validator)\n    extracted = subprocess.run(['pdftotext', '-layout', 'paper.pdf', '-'], check=True, capture_output=True, text=True)\n    assert not validator.validate_rendered_supplementary_information(extracted.stdout.split('\\f'))\n    recorded_inputs = []\n    system_roots = [Path(path).resolve() for path in ('/etc/texmf', '/usr/share/texmf', '/usr/share/texlive', '/var/lib/texmf')]\n    for line in Path('paper.fls').read_text().splitlines():\n        if not line.startswith('INPUT '):\n            continue\n        resolved = Path(line[6:]).resolve()\n        assert resolved.is_relative_to(root) or any(resolved.is_relative_to(system_root) for system_root in system_roots), str(resolved)\n        recorded_inputs.append(str(resolved))\n    last_body = document[reference_index-1]\n    bounds = [span['bbox'] for block in last_body.get_text('dict')['blocks'] if block['type'] == 0\n              for line in block['lines'] for span in line['spans']\n              if span['bbox'][0] >= 107 and 65 < span['bbox'][1] < 715]\n    report = {\n        'status': 'independent_artifact_checks_passed', 'hard_errors': [],\n        'scope': 'Local source, canonical schemas, rendered PDF, retained-metric consistency and evidence links; not a claim that unavailable parent orchestration checks ran.',\n        'body_pages': reference_index, 'total_pages': len(document),\n        'references_start_page': reference_index+1, 'supplement_start_page': supplement_index+1,\n        'reference_count': len(cited), 'claim_count': len(claims), 'figure_count': len(actual),\n        'dangling_evidence_references': verified['summary']['dangling_references'],\n        'last_body_content_bounds_pt': [min(bound[1] for bound in bounds), max(bound[3] for bound in bounds)],\n        'last_body_fill_note': 'Bounds are descriptive, not the authoritative parent geometric-occupancy verdict. Body has nine pages, so the special eight-page minimum-fill condition is not invoked.',\n        'compiled_inputs_union_check': {'passed': True, 'recorded_input_count': len(recorded_inputs)},\n        'qualification': summary['qualification'],\n        'environment_limitations': [\n            'Canonical validate_figures.py cannot import src.orchestrator.paper_step in this isolated workspace. The shipped canonical figure schema, required figure IDs, source paths and strategy density budgets were checked independently.',\n            'Canonical compile_latex.sh input guard rejects /usr/share/texmf/web2c/texmf.cnf because it is a system symlink into a different approved system tree. No validator or system symlink was modified. Sanitized pdflatex/bibtex passes compiled the PDF; all recorded inputs independently resolve inside the workspace or the union of approved system TeX roots.'\n        ],\n        'orchestrator_pending': ['Replace the intentional conceptual-overview placeholder and prompt-log stub with the synchronous concept render, then perform the parent final compile and authoritative layout checks.']\n    }\n    Path('validation_report.json').write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=2))\n    print(json.dumps(report, indent=2))\n    template_source = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ICLR/Master-Template/master/iclr2026/'\n    Path('template_provenance.json').write_text(json.dumps({\n        'venue': 'ICLR 2026', 'anonymous_review': True,\n        'files': [{'path': name, 'source_url': template_source+name,\n                   'sha256': hashlib.sha256(Path(name).read_bytes()).hexdigest()}\n                  for name in ('iclr2026_conference.sty', 'iclr2026_conference.bst')]}, indent=2))\n{\n  \"schema_name\": \"scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest\",\n  \"artifact\": {\n    \"path\": \"paper.tex\",\n    \"kind\": \"manuscript\"\n  },\n  \"derived_from\": [\n    \"@evidence[[paper_data.json]]\",\n    \"@evidence[[claims_grounding.json]]\",\n    \"@evidence[[references.bib]]\",\n    \"@evidence[[source_evidence/selected_model.py]]\",\n    \"@evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py]]\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"Manuscript authored during the paper-writing workflow; this sidecar records its source trail, not an automated manuscript generator.\"\n}{\n  \"schema_name\": \"scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest\",\n  \"artifact\": {\n    \"path\": \"claims_grounding.json\",\n    \"kind\": \"derived\"\n  },\n  \"derived_from\": [\n    \"@evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\",\n    \"@evidence[[analysis/summary.json]]\",\n    \"@evidence[[references_provenance.json]]\",\n    \"@evidence[[source_evidence/selected_model.py]]\"\n  ],\n  \"generated_by\": {\n    \"script_path\": \"build_claims.py\"\n  }\n}import json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\ndef main():\n    data = json.loads(Path('paper_data.json').read_text())\n    summary = json.loads(Path('analysis/summary.json').read_text())\n    provenance = json.loads(Path('references_provenance.json').read_text())\n    evidence_anchor = '@evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]'\n    claims = []\n\n    def add(claim, source_ids=None, supporting_artifacts=None, locator=None, citation_keys=None):\n        entry = {'claim': claim, 'source_ids': source_ids or ['final.evidence.episodes'],\n                 'citation_keys': citation_keys or []}\n        if supporting_artifacts:\n            entry['supporting_artifacts'] = supporting_artifacts\n        if locator:\n            entry['evidence_locator'] = locator\n        claims.append(entry)\n\n    add('The independent final evaluation completed, was qualified, and reports successful specified checks; qualification is not a superiority or shifted-validity result.',\n        ['final.qualification.status', 'final.qualification.outcome', 'final.qualification.correct', 'final.metric.control_check_pass_rate'])\n    add('The final study comprises eight seeds, six conditions (logistic-normal IID, Dirichlet IID, shifted Dirichlet at K=3 and 8), and alpha=0.05,0.10,0.20. All recorded cases are complete.',\n        supporting_artifacts=['source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:37', 'source_evidence/data_manifest.json'],\n        locator='/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes')\n    add('Final seeds are 1009,1013,1019,1021,1031,1033,1039,1049; train/calibration/test sizes are 1024/512/2048 with six covariates.',\n        supporting_artifacts=['source_evidence/data_manifest.json', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:727'])\n    implementation_claims = [\n        ('Positive observed continuous compositions, not categorical labels or latent probabilities, are the response. The fixed Helmert ILR basis has K-1 coordinates.', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py:37'),\n        ('The design uses intercept, raw features, squares, sines and x0*x1. Center and log-residual ridge penalties are 1 and 10; intercept penalty is 1e-8; residual floor is .02.', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py:98'),\n        ('Centers are clipped to [-100,100] and positive base and corrected scales to [1e-4,100]. The base log-residual fit uses in-sample residuals; correction moments are cross-fitted.', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py:114'),\n        ('Three-fold training permutations use random seed 0. Moment features use standard deviation floor 1e-8; standardized residuals use scale floor 1e-4; queries are batched in 128 rows.', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py:109'),\n        ('Local moments average squared standardized ILR residuals over K-1 coordinates, Gaussian-smooth them over standardized covariates, and shrink the ratio toward 1 by prior mass.', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py:133'),\n        ('Moment ratios are clipped to [.25,4]; a common row-scalar multiplies all ILR scales, preserving their within-row ratios. The correction blends are 0,.5,1; bandwidths .5*sqrt(6),sqrt(6); prior masses 10,50.', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py:172'),\n        ('Nested three-fold training selection uses swapped pseudo-calibration/evaluation halves; the row-weighted alpha-averaged log arithmetic mean ILR-box volume is minimized, with smaller blend breaking ties.', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py:275'),\n        ('The selector uses exact finite ranks, Gaussian-loss fallback for unavailable ranks or invalid radii/objectives, and a neutral tiny-sample fallback. Realized fallback frequencies and selected settings are not retained.', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py:188'),\n        ('Global constant scale multiplication cancels its conformal radius, apart from clipping. At alpha .05, 18 internal calibration observations are insufficient for a finite rank; 19 suffice. Numerical invariance assertions are source checks, not a scientific ablation.', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py:237'),\n        ('Independent final calibration uses ceil((m+1)*(1-alpha)) order statistic with infinity when unavailable, and closed membership. It is not selected on calibration labels.', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:836'),\n        ('The unscaled ILR comparator sets scales to one at the same center. Simplex max uses a joint coordinate maximum. Bonferroni calibrates K simplex coordinates at alpha/K, not ILR coordinates.', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:857'),\n        ('Mass is uniform-simplex probability content estimated at 128 test contexts using 1024 shared Dirichlet(1) probes; utility equals (1-mass)*max(0,1-absolute_coverage_error/(1-alpha)). Errors are absolute before averaging.', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:727'),\n        ('IID covariates are uniform on [-1.5,1.5]^6, logistic-normal noise standard deviation is .25, Dirichlet concentration is 4+35/(1+exp(2*x0)), and gamma coordinates are floored at 1e-12 before closure.', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:727'),\n        ('The fixed mean is .7*sin(XW)+.3*x0*cos(j), with W[l,j]=sin(l*(K-1)+j+1)/3. Shift changes only test X to clipped N(.8,1) in [-2.5,3], changing covariate support as well as frequency.', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:727'),\n        ('Independent random streams use SeedSequence([seed,case,split,202611]); reference split index is 3. Frozen resources are checked for numeric row-content disjointness, positivity, closure and hashes.', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:727'),\n        ('Per-context mass resolution is 1/1024. Zero hits have a one-sided .95 upper bound 1-.05**(1/1024)=.00292124, not zero mass. Averaged plugin context standard errors do not quantify joint mass uncertainty.', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:905'),\n        ('The evaluator resamples seed blocks 20000 times using RNG seed 62845. Paired utility intervals have optional tail probability .05/(2*54); volume intervals are unadjusted. Repeated uncertainty summaries are deduplicated.', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:1036'),\n        ('Constant-input queries use training-mean features; nonidentity permutations rotate calibration and test rows separately. Whole-simplex and zero-radius references are degenerate metric controls, not useful calibrated baselines.', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:929'),\n        ('The evaluated environment requires CPython 3.11 or 3.12 and NumPy 1.26.4 with native Linux isolation. No external dataset is downloaded for the synthetic study.', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:1186'),\n    ]\n    for text, artifact in implementation_claims:\n        add(text, ['final.evidence.episodes', 'result.top_program_01'], [artifact])\n    add('The matched final evidence does not contain a selector-only Gaussian-versus-rank comparison or an original-initializer comparison. The earlier configurations are development evidence, not final ablations.',\n        ['final.evidence.episodes', 'result.top_program_01', 'result.top_program_02', 'result.top_program_03'],\n        ['source_evidence/selected_model.py:275', 'source_evidence/development_gaussian.py:185',\n         'source_evidence/development_joint.py:152', 'paper_data.json'])\n    add('IID and shifted scaled-ILR absolute coverage errors are 0.013562011718750005 and 0.13034261067708333, respectively.',\n        ['final.metric.iid_coverage_error', 'final.metric.shift_coverage_error'])\n    add('The scaled-ILR mean utility is 0.661819668104677, mass 0.3034934467739529, and aggregate utility gap to the strongest standard comparator is 0.011594669497844157.',\n        ['final.metric.final_score', 'final.metric.mean_volume', 'final.metric.baseline_utility_gap'])\n    for method, values in summary['methods'].items():\n        add('Main summary table, ' + method + ': ' + json.dumps(values),\n            supporting_artifacts=['analysis/summary.json', 'build_analysis.py'], locator='analysis/summary.json#/methods/' + method)\n    for baseline, values in summary['paired_overall'].items():\n        add('New retained-data descriptive paired aggregate utility contrast, scaled ILR minus ' + baseline + ': ' + json.dumps(values),\n            supporting_artifacts=['analysis/summary.json', 'build_analysis.py'], locator='analysis/summary.json#/paired_overall/' + baseline)\n    for case, values in summary['coverage'].items():\n        rows = []\n        for alpha_index, alpha in enumerate(summary['alphas']):\n            per_seed = [next(item for item in episode['solution']['cases'] if item['case'] == case)['methods']['scaled_ilr'][alpha_index]\n                        for episode in data['final_evaluation']['evaluation_evidence']['episodes']]\n            rows.append({'alpha': alpha, 'mass': sum(item['volume'] for item in per_seed)/len(per_seed),\n                         'utility': sum(item['utility'] for item in per_seed)/len(per_seed)})\n        add('Supplementary scaled-ILR mass and utility means for ' + case + ': ' + json.dumps(rows),\n            supporting_artifacts=['analysis/coverage_table.tex', 'build_analysis.py'])\n        add('Coverage figure, text and extended table for ' + case + ': ' + json.dumps(values),\n            supporting_artifacts=['analysis/summary.json', 'build_analysis.py'], locator='analysis/summary.json#/coverage/' + case)\n        for baseline, comparisons in summary['retained_uncertainty'][case]['paired_baselines'].items():\n            add('Complete paired utility/mass contrasts for ' + case + ', scaled ILR minus ' + baseline + ': ' + json.dumps(comparisons),\n                supporting_artifacts=['analysis/summary.json'],\n                locator='/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes/0/solution/seed_block_uncertainty/' + case + '/paired_baselines/' + baseline)\n    for group, values in summary['feature_groups_alpha_010'].items():\n        add('Descriptive sign-of-x0 group mean coverage at alpha .10, ' + group + ': ' + json.dumps(values),\n            supporting_artifacts=['analysis/summary.json', 'build_analysis.py'])\n    add('Additional coverage, overall utility and group intervals resample all seed blocks jointly 20000 times at bootstrap seed 20261117, retaining condition and level dependence.',\n        supporting_artifacts=['analysis/summary.json', 'build_analysis.py'])\n    add('Favorable simplex-baseline contrasts concentrate in IID Dirichlet K8; all shifted utility differences are negative and all shifted mass differences positive. This is not uniform dominance.',\n        supporting_artifacts=['analysis/summary.json#/retained_uncertainty'])\n    for reference in provenance['references']:\n        add('Background citation: ' + reference['title'] + '; access scope: ' + reference['read_scope'],\n            [reference['id']], [reference['read_artifact']], citation_keys=[reference['citation_key']])\n    add('Independent split-conformal marginal coverage follows the standard exchangeable-score rank argument conditional on training, not exact realized, feature-conditional, or shifted coverage.',\n        ['ref.Lei2018', 'ref.Angelopoulos2021'], ['source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:836'], citation_keys=['Lei2018'])\n    claims_path = Path('claims_grounding.json')\n    claims_path.write_text(json.dumps({'claims': claims}, indent=2))\n    sidecar = {'schema_name': 'scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest',\n               'artifact': {'path': 'claims_grounding.json', 'kind': 'derived'},\n               'derived_from': [evidence_anchor, '@evidence[[analysis/summary.json]]',\n                                '@evidence[[references_provenance.json]]', '@evidence[[source_evidence/selected_model.py]]'],\n               'generated_by': {'script_path': 'build_claims.py'}}\n    Path('claims_grounding.json.prov.json').write_text(json.dumps(sidecar, indent=2))\n    print('Mapped', len(claims), 'claims; qualification independently:', summary['qualification'])\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
