{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,42p' build_claims.py; sed -n '84,145p' validate_artifacts.py; sed -n '1,100p' .codex/skills/retrieve-references/SKILL.md; cat literature/access_notes.md | tail -22; cat final_validation.log\"","aggregated_output":"import json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\ndef main():\n    data = json.loads(Path('paper_data.json').read_text())\n    summary = json.loads(Path('analysis/summary.json').read_text())\n    provenance = json.loads(Path('references_provenance.json').read_text())\n    evidence_anchor = '@evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]'\n    claims = []\n\n    def add(claim, source_ids=None, supporting_artifacts=None, locator=None, citation_keys=None):\n        entry = {'claim': claim, 'source_ids': source_ids or ['final.evidence.episodes'],\n                 'citation_keys': citation_keys or []}\n        if supporting_artifacts:\n            entry['supporting_artifacts'] = supporting_artifacts\n        if locator:\n            entry['evidence_locator'] = locator\n        claims.append(entry)\n\n    add('The independent final evaluation completed, was qualified, and reports successful specified checks; qualification is not a superiority or shifted-validity result.',\n        ['final.qualification.status', 'final.qualification.outcome', 'final.qualification.correct', 'final.metric.control_check_pass_rate'])\n    add('The final study comprises eight seeds, six conditions (logistic-normal IID, Dirichlet IID, shifted Dirichlet at K=3 and 8), and alpha=0.05,0.10,0.20. All recorded cases are complete.',\n        supporting_artifacts=['source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:37', 'source_evidence/data_manifest.json'],\n        locator='/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes')\n    add('Final seeds are 1009,1013,1019,1021,1031,1033,1039,1049; train/calibration/test sizes are 1024/512/2048 with six covariates.',\n        supporting_artifacts=['source_evidence/data_manifest.json', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:727'])\n    implementation_claims = [\n        ('Positive observed continuous compositions, not categorical labels or latent probabilities, are the response. The fixed Helmert ILR basis has K-1 coordinates.', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py:37'),\n        ('The design uses intercept, raw features, squares, sines and x0*x1. Center and log-residual ridge penalties are 1 and 10; intercept penalty is 1e-8; residual floor is .02.', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py:98'),\n        ('Centers are clipped to [-100,100] and positive base and corrected scales to [1e-4,100]. The base log-residual fit uses in-sample residuals; correction moments are cross-fitted.', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py:114'),\n        ('Three-fold training permutations use random seed 0. Moment features use standard deviation floor 1e-8; standardized residuals use scale floor 1e-4; queries are batched in 128 rows.', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py:109'),\n        ('Local moments average squared standardized ILR residuals over K-1 coordinates, Gaussian-smooth them over standardized covariates, and shrink the ratio toward 1 by prior mass.', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py:133'),\n        ('Moment ratios are clipped to [.25,4]; a common row-scalar multiplies all ILR scales, preserving their within-row ratios. The correction blends are 0,.5,1; bandwidths .5*sqrt(6),sqrt(6); prior masses 10,50.', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py:172'),\n        ('Nested three-fold training selection uses swapped pseudo-calibration/evaluation halves; the row-weighted alpha-averaged log arithmetic mean ILR-box volume is minimized, with smaller blend breaking ties.', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py:275'),\n        ('The selector uses exact finite ranks, Gaussian-loss fallback for unavailable ranks or invalid radii/objectives, and a neutral tiny-sample fallback. Realized fallback frequencies and selected settings are not retained.', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py:188'),\n        ('Global constant scale multiplication cancels its conformal radius, apart from clipping. At alpha .05, 18 internal calibration observations are insufficient for a finite rank; 19 suffice. Numerical invariance assertions are source checks, not a scientific ablation.', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py:237'),\n        ('Independent final calibration uses ceil((m+1)*(1-alpha)) order statistic with infinity when unavailable, and closed membership. It is not selected on calibration labels.', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:836'),\n        ('The unscaled ILR comparator sets scales to one at the same center. Simplex max uses a joint coordinate maximum. Bonferroni calibrates K simplex coordinates at alpha/K, not ILR coordinates.', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:857'),\n        ('Mass is uniform-simplex probability content estimated at 128 test contexts using 1024 shared Dirichlet(1) probes; utility equals (1-mass)*max(0,1-absolute_coverage_error/(1-alpha)). Errors are absolute before averaging.', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:727'),\n        ('IID covariates are uniform on [-1.5,1.5]^6, logistic-normal noise standard deviation is .25, Dirichlet concentration is 4+35/(1+exp(2*x0)), and gamma coordinates are floored at 1e-12 before closure.', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:727'),\n        ('The fixed mean is .7*sin(XW)+.3*x0*cos(j), with W[l,j]=sin(l*(K-1)+j+1)/3. Shift changes only test X to clipped N(.8,1) in [-2.5,3], changing covariate support as well as frequency.', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:727'),\n    specification = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('rendered_si', validator_path)\n    validator = importlib.util.module_from_spec(specification)\n    specification.loader.exec_module(validator)\n    extracted = subprocess.run(['pdftotext', '-layout', 'paper.pdf', '-'], check=True, capture_output=True, text=True)\n    assert not validator.validate_rendered_supplementary_information(extracted.stdout.split('\\f'))\n    recorded_inputs = []\n    system_roots = [Path(path).resolve() for path in ('/etc/texmf', '/usr/share/texmf', '/usr/share/texlive', '/var/lib/texmf')]\n    for line in Path('paper.fls').read_text().splitlines():\n        if not line.startswith('INPUT '):\n            continue\n        resolved = Path(line[6:]).resolve()\n        assert resolved.is_relative_to(root) or any(resolved.is_relative_to(system_root) for system_root in system_roots), str(resolved)\n        recorded_inputs.append(str(resolved))\n    last_body = document[reference_index-1]\n    bounds = [span['bbox'] for block in last_body.get_text('dict')['blocks'] if block['type'] == 0\n              for line in block['lines'] for span in line['spans']\n              if span['bbox'][0] >= 107 and 65 < span['bbox'][1] < 715]\n    report = {\n        'status': 'independent_artifact_checks_passed', 'hard_errors': [],\n        'scope': 'Local source, canonical schemas, rendered PDF, retained-metric consistency and evidence links; not a claim that unavailable parent orchestration checks ran.',\n        'body_pages': reference_index, 'total_pages': len(document),\n        'references_start_page': reference_index+1, 'supplement_start_page': supplement_index+1,\n        'reference_count': len(cited), 'claim_count': len(claims), 'figure_count': len(actual),\n        'dangling_evidence_references': verified['summary']['dangling_references'],\n        'last_body_content_bounds_pt': [min(bound[1] for bound in bounds), max(bound[3] for bound in bounds)],\n        'last_body_fill_note': 'Bounds are descriptive, not the authoritative parent geometric-occupancy verdict. Body has nine pages, so the special eight-page minimum-fill condition is not invoked.',\n        'compiled_inputs_union_check': {'passed': True, 'recorded_input_count': len(recorded_inputs)},\n        'qualification': summary['qualification'],\n        'environment_limitations': [\n            'Canonical validate_figures.py cannot import src.orchestrator.paper_step in this isolated workspace. The shipped canonical figure schema, required figure IDs, source paths and strategy density budgets were checked independently.',\n            'Canonical compile_latex.sh input guard rejects /usr/share/texmf/web2c/texmf.cnf because it is a system symlink into a different approved system tree. No validator or system symlink was modified. Sanitized pdflatex/bibtex passes compiled the PDF; all recorded inputs independently resolve inside the workspace or the union of approved system TeX roots.'\n        ],\n        'orchestrator_pending': ['Replace the intentional conceptual-overview placeholder and prompt-log stub with the synchronous concept render, then perform the parent final compile and authoritative layout checks.']\n    }\n    Path('validation_report.json').write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=2))\n    print(json.dumps(report, indent=2))\n    template_source = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ICLR/Master-Template/master/iclr2026/'\n    Path('template_provenance.json').write_text(json.dumps({\n        'venue': 'ICLR 2026', 'anonymous_review': True,\n        'files': [{'path': name, 'source_url': template_source+name,\n                   'sha256': hashlib.sha256(Path(name).read_bytes()).hexdigest()}\n                  for name in ('iclr2026_conference.sty', 'iclr2026_conference.bst')]}, indent=2))\n    for name, kind, sources in [\n        ('paper.tex', 'manuscript', ['paper_data.json', 'claims_grounding.json', 'references.bib', 'source_evidence/selected_model.py', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py']),\n        ('paper.pdf', 'manuscript', ['paper.tex', 'references.bib', 'figure_manifest.json']),\n        ('figure_manifest.json', 'derived', ['paper_strategy.json', 'build_analysis.py']),\n        ('validation_report.json', 'derived', ['paper.tex', 'paper.pdf', 'scientific-evidence/verification-report.json'])]:\n        sidecar = {'schema_name': 'scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest',\n                   'artifact': {'path': name, 'kind': kind},\n                   'derived_from': ['@'+'evidence[['+source+']]' for source in sources]}\n        if name == 'paper.pdf':\n            sidecar['generated_by'] = {\n                'script_path': '.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_compile_inputs.py',\n                'command': ['python', '.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_compile_inputs.py',\n                            'run', '--', 'pdflatex', '-recorder', '-no-shell-escape',\n                            '-interaction=nonstopmode', '-halt-on-error', 'paper.tex']}\n        elif name != 'paper.tex':\n            sidecar['generated_by'] = {'script_path': 'build_analysis.py' if name == 'figure_manifest.json' else 'validate_artifacts.py'}\n        else:\n            sidecar['notes'] = 'Manuscript authored during the paper-writing workflow; this sidecar records its source trail, not an automated manuscript generator.'\n        Path(name+'.prov.json').write_text(json.dumps(sidecar, indent=2))\n\n---\nname: retrieve-references\ndescription: Retrieve grounded BibTeX references from Semantic Scholar Graph API, OpenAlex, or Google Scholar (`scholarly`) and write references.bib plus provenance JSON for paper generation.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nFetch references from Semantic Scholar Graph API, OpenAlex, or Google Scholar (via `scholarly`) and keep only real BibTeX entries.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- Final report/paper generation.\n- Related-work section needs grounded citations.\n\n# What to do\n1. Build focused search queries from task goal, method names, and top experiment ideas.\n2. Preferred path (Semantic Scholar Graph API):\n```bash\npython scripts/s2_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n3. Fallback path (OpenAlex):\n```bash\npython scripts/openalex_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --search-limit 10 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n   Optional:\n   - `--mailto you@example.com` to enter the OpenAlex polite pool\n   - Env fallback: `OPENALEX_EMAIL`\n4. Alternate path (Google Scholar API wrapper with `scholarly`):\n```bash\npython -m pip install scholarly\npython scripts/scholarly_fetch.py \\\n  --query \"query one\" \\\n  --query \"query two\" \\\n  --min-refs 8 \\\n  --max-refs 15 \\\n  --search-limit 25 \\\n  --sort-by relevance \\\n  --proxy-mode auto \\\n  --delay-seconds 0.5 \\\n  --out-bib references.bib \\\n  --out-json references_provenance.json\n```\n   Proxy options:\n   - `--proxy-mode auto|none|free|single`\n   - `--proxy-http <url>` / `--proxy-https <url>` for `single`\n   - Env fallbacks: `SCHOLARLY_PROXY_MODE`, `SCHOLARLY_PROXY_HTTP`, `SCHOLARLY_PROXY_HTTPS`\n   - Global `HTTP_PROXY` / `HTTPS_PROXY` are intentionally ignored to avoid accidental ambient proxying\n5. Require `S2_API_KEY` when available for `s2_fetch.py` (script reads env automatically).\n6. Keep only references with valid BibTeX and citation key.\n7. Dedupe by citation key and paper id.\n8. Fail hard if references found `< min-refs`.\n9. Use `s2_fetch.py` first for stability, `openalex_fetch.py` as the next fallback, and `scholarly_fetch.py` last if the other sources fail.\n\n# Outputs\n- `references.bib`\n- `references_provenance.json`\n\n# Notes\n- Use `templates/provenance.schema.json` for expected shape.\n# Literature access scope\n\nThe 25 cited sources are exactly those listed in `references_provenance.json`. The visible literature discussion uses broad claims supported by the inspected abstracts or publisher excerpts, not uninspected detailed results. The ILR construction and experiment definitions are additionally supported by readable local code, and the calibration rank argument is stated explicitly rather than quoting an uninspected theorem number.\n\nThe direct Springer pages for the conformal monograph, inductive regression chapter, conditional-validity article, and ILR article were consulted only for their overview/abstract and bibliographic identity. The Wiley book excerpt was read on its introductory pages. The PMLR density-estimator paper was checked against its official abstract and citation metadata. Other abstracts were read from their directly identified arXiv or metadata records.\n\nNo citation links, related-article recommendations, or joint conformal/composition discovery searches were followed. No prohibited study was identified, discussed, or used. An initially mistyped arXiv identifier returned an unrelated metabolic-network abstract; it was rejected, and the correct conditional-validity source was subsequently checked directly. Exact-title search also produced unrelated DOI matches or reprint versions for some classical works; these were corrected or excluded rather than silently treated as the intended sources. Excluded Watson/Wilson lookup records are kept under `rejected/` solely as retrieval audit material and are not cited.\n{\n  \"status\": \"independent_artifact_checks_passed\",\n  \"hard_errors\": [],\n  \"scope\": \"Local source, canonical schemas, rendered PDF, retained-metric consistency and evidence links; not a claim that unavailable parent orchestration checks ran.\",\n  \"body_pages\": 9,\n  \"total_pages\": 16,\n  \"references_start_page\": 10,\n  \"supplement_start_page\": 12,\n  \"reference_count\": 25,\n  \"claim_count\": 102,\n  \"figure_count\": 4,\n  \"dangling_evidence_references\": 0,\n  \"last_body_content_bounds_pt\": [\n    84.17748260498047,\n    572.6866455078125\n  ],\n  \"last_body_fill_note\": \"Bounds are descriptive, not the authoritative parent geometric-occupancy verdict. Body has nine pages, so the special eight-page minimum-fill condition is not invoked.\",\n  \"compiled_inputs_union_check\": {\n    \"passed\": true,\n    \"recorded_input_count\": 262\n  },\n  \"qualification\": {\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"outcome\": \"qualified\",\n    \"correct\": true\n  },\n  \"environment_limitations\": [\n    \"Canonical validate_figures.py cannot import src.orchestrator.paper_step in this isolated workspace. The shipped canonical figure schema, required figure IDs, source paths and strategy density budgets were checked independently.\",\n    \"Canonical compile_latex.sh input guard rejects /usr/share/texmf/web2c/texmf.cnf because it is a system symlink into a different approved system tree. No validator or system symlink was modified. Sanitized pdflatex/bibtex passes compiled the PDF; all recorded inputs independently resolve inside the workspace or the union of approved system TeX roots.\"\n  ],\n  \"orchestrator_pending\": [\n    \"Replace the intentional conceptual-overview placeholder and prompt-log stub with the synchronous concept render, then perform the parent final compile and authoritative layout checks.\"\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
